# ZoneWise configuration. Copy to .env and edit. .env is never committed.
# Every variable here is optional except the API key: the default in app/config.py is
# used when a variable is unset or blank, and a value that will not parse falls back to
# that default rather than stopping the server (D-063, D-065).

# --- the provider and the model ------------------------------------------------------
# Which service answers: anthropic or groq. Default: anthropic. Everything that depends
# on a key follows this one setting — the key that is checked, the default model, the
# 503 from /api/ask, the banner in the web app — so a Groq key with LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# reads as no key rather than as a key that will 401 (D-082). A value that is neither
# name falls back to anthropic, and /api/health reports the provider actually in use.
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic

# The Anthropic API key, used when LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic. Without a usable key for the
# configured provider the app runs in search-only mode: the map, the zone lookup, clause
# search and the clause reader all work, and /api/ask and /api/agent return 503 with the
# retrieved clauses in the body.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-key-here

# The Groq API key, used when LLM_PROVIDER=groq. Keys start with gsk_ and a client
# refuses to be built unless yours does and is at least 40 characters long, for the
# same reason the Anthropic check is strict (D-040).
# Get one at https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=your-key-here

# Which model answers. The default follows the provider:
#   anthropic   claude-haiku-5-5       (Anthropic's current Haiku API model id)
#   groq        openai/gpt-oss-120b    (an open-weights reasoning model, free tier)
# Override to try another model without touching the code. `uv run python -m app.llm`
# lists the models your key may use and says whether this one is among them.
# LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# The smallest gap between two LLM calls, in seconds. Default: 0, no pacing, which is
# right for a one-question interface. A batch run sets it to stay inside a provider's
# requests-per-minute limit: scripts/live_run.py uses 2.5, which is 24 requests a
# minute against Groq's free-tier 30 (D-082).
# LLM_MIN_INTERVAL_S=0

# Force the scripted FakeLLM even when a real key is present. Useful for a demo that
# must not spend anything. Default: false.
# ZONEWISE_USE_FAKE_LLM=0

# --- the question verification screen ----------------------------------------------
# 1 enables the dev-only endpoints under /api/dev/eval/ and the Verify tab in the web
# app. Anything else, including unset, makes them 404. Never set this in production.
# Default: false.
# ZONEWISE_DEV=0

# --- abstention ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which score decides that retrieval was too weak to ask the model at all:
#   dense_cosine   top-1 dense cosine similarity (the default)
#   rerank_score   top-1 cross-encoder score, only meaningful when USE_RERANKER=1
# ABSTAIN_SIGNAL=dense_cosine

# The cut-off for that signal. PROVISIONAL (D-071): it is set so that it refuses none
# of the drafted answerable questions, which is the most conservative choice available
# before the questions are verified. The final value comes from the sweep in
# eval/run_eval.py against eval/questions_verified.jsonl.
#
# The two signals are on completely different scales, so this MUST be reset whenever
# ABSTAIN_SIGNAL changes: a cosine similarity runs 0 to 1, a cross-encoder score runs
# about -11 to +11. The provisional value for each, from scripts/tune_abstention.py:
#   dense_cosine    0.5804
#   rerank_score  -10.2377
# ABSTAIN_THRESHOLD=0.5804

# Rerank the top 20 results with a cross-encoder after location-aware fusion. Off until
# the evaluation shows it helps (D-070). Measured at 2.4 s a query against 0.031 s
# without it, so turning it on is a real trade and not a free improvement.
# USE_RERANKER=0

# --- the semantic claim check --------------------------------------------------------
# What happens to the claim check's verdicts. After a valid answer it makes one extra
# call, showing the model each sentence beside the full text of the clauses that
# sentence cites, and asking whether the clause states it (D-096). The citation check
# is structural and cannot ask that question; this is the semantic half.
#   off       no second call at all
#   shadow    the verdicts go in the response and the request log; the answer is
#             untouched, whatever they say.
#   enforce   a sentence judged "unsupported" is dropped, and the answer is thrown away
#             with abstain_reason=unsupported_claims when the first sentence goes or
#             nothing is left. THE DEFAULT since the v3 verdicts were read (D-103).
# It is a model checking a model, so it is evidence and not proof. What the v3 shadow
# run showed: of 39 sentences it called 1 unsupported, and that call was right; it
# flagged no correct sentence. It costs about 1,377 tokens per answer. What it does not
# catch: a sentence rated "partly" is kept, which is how a wrong figure or a missing
# condition survives it (demo-14, demo-06). See D-103.
# SUPPORT_CHECK=enforce

# --- limits and origins --------------------------------------------------------------
# Answering requests allowed per IP address per minute. Default: 10.
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=10

# Answering requests allowed for the whole service per day. This is the one that stands
# between a bug and an unbounded bill. Default: 300.
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_DAY=300

# Which browser origins may call the API, comma-separated. Default: the Vite dev server.
# In production set this to your own site and nothing else.
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# The longest question the API accepts, in characters. Default: 500.
# MAX_QUESTION_CHARS=500

# The largest request body the API accepts, in bytes. Default: 65536.
# MAX_REQUEST_BYTES=65536
